  "Notes": "Polarising beamsplitter in glass at 45 degrees, 1064 nm\n\nCaveats:\n- Manufacturability is scored with MINT/MAXT (minimum and maximum layer thickness) at a low weight. A sensitivity term (SENS) would score robustness to thickness errors directly, but it needs second derivatives of the merit function and is not offered; MINT/MAXT keep layers depositable and have exact derivatives.\n- Rs and Tp are asked for separately. When the polarisation split itself is the specification, an R_NPOL target expresses it as one operand with a well-conditioned gradient toward balance.",
